有昆仑万维、商汤、百度、蚂蚁、minimax、亚马逊云科技、京东等领军企业代表齐聚现场；也有复旦大学特聘教授邱锡鹏、香港大学助理教授黄超等顶尖学者带来前沿技术研判；还有盛大evermind、太初元碁、风行在线、轻松健康集团、趣丸科技、colaos\u0026amp;marswave、evomap等一线实战玩家分享落地经验；以及硅谷fusionfund创始合伙人张璐带来ai产业与算力赛道新视角。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e与此同时，量子位重磅揭晓了“2026年度值得关注的aigc企业”与“2026年度值得关注的aigc产品”两大奖项，并同步发布了《2026年中国ai应用全景图谱报告》。\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cpclass=\"image-wrapper\"\u003e\u003cimgdata-img-size-val=\"1265,843\"src=\"https://img.36krcdn.com/hsossms/20260520/v2_7915873cb5fe4fe38567c9416bd76969@6381723_oswg1124974oswg1265oswg843_img_png?x-oss-process=image/quality,q_90/format,jpg/interlace,1\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003e锚定技术革新，洞察行业发展核心趋势\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003e2026年，aiagent已从行业讨论的热点，演变为企业与开发者必须直面的现实议题。本届峰会上，多位大咖从不同视角拆解了agent落地的关键路径与挑战。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e昆仑万维董事长兼ceo方汉从一线视角回答了“个人和企业如何应对agent冲击”，他表示冲击是真实的，但关键不是要不要被冲击，而是怎么度过过渡期。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e亚马逊云科技产品技术部技术总监王晓野则聚焦“跨越agent落地鸿沟”，拆解从顶级大模型到企业级aiagent之间的工程化挑战与解决方案。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e香港大学助理教授、博士生导师黄超结合学术前沿视角，探讨了aiagent范式变革带来的技术机遇与行业挑战。\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e盛大集团副总裁、evermindceo邓亚峰分享了长期记忆驱动的自进化技术，阐释ai如何从工具型应用，演化为可持续成长的数字生产力系统。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e在agent成为行业焦点的同时，为其提供底层支撑的大模型本身也在不断突破能力边界。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e商汤科技执行副总裁、首席科学家林达华深入分析了“从多模态统一到空间智能：迈向可感知、可生成、可行动的ai新前沿”。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e京东joyinside业务负责人戴文军则将这一命题进一步推向物理世界，分享了ai从屏幕里走出来，走进真实终端、真实场景。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e复旦大学特聘教授、上海创智学院院长助理、模思智能创始人邱锡鹏带来了moss多模态大模型最新研发成果，分享了前沿技术的优化思路。\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003e深耕细分赛道，一线玩家分享落地实战\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003e具体到不同领域，机会究竟何在？本次峰会上，众多ai赛道的实战玩家给出了答案。他们带来了全行业可落地、可借鉴的成熟应用案例。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e风行在线ceo易正朝提出核心判断，认为从ai编程赋能开发创作，到ai视频革新内容生产，“众创才是ai生产力的核心杠杆”。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e百度秒哒产品总经理朱广翔分享了“人人都是创造者”的产品理念，展示了想象力释放生产力、ai赋能普通用户降本提效的全新模式。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eminimaxtob中国区商业化负责人胡维琦以“intelligencewitheveryone”为题，分享了minimax在过去一年中的真实打法与思考。\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e轻松健康集团执行副总裁马孝武则立足健康垂直领域，以“从循证智能体到ai驱动的健康服务增长飞轮”为题，阐述了以ai为核心的新型健康服务能力。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e此外，ai基础设施的范式重构也是今年大会关注的主线之一。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003efusionfund创始合伙人张璐立足全球资本与产业的双重视角，提出“算力叙事重构”，深度解读了从训练到推理的ai基础设施新范式。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e太初元碁首席产品官、高级副总裁洪源则以“国产ai算力筑基token智能新未来”为题，探寻国产算力适配新时代ai产业的发展路径。\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003egenaitalk+agent圆桌思辨\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003e大咖主题演讲环节之外，大会今年还安排了一场重磅genaitalk和一场观点密集的agent圆桌。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003egenaitalk环节\u003c/strong\u003e，蚂蚁灵波科技首席科学家沈宇军与量子位联合创始人兼总编辑李根，围绕核心命题“ai2.0下半场，从aigc到aiga”展开深度对谈。\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e对谈中，沈宇军回顾了过去几年aigc在文本、图像、视频等领域的快速演进，并判断ai2.0已进入下半场，正从aigc向aiga跃迁。\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：全球AI技术大会 2026\n\n网页标题：AI Events Around the World in 2026: The Main Annual Meetings To Know\n\n网页链接：https://justainews.com/ai-compliance/ai-research/artificial-intelligence-events-2026/\n\n发布时间：2026-05-14T00:00:00+08:00\n\n网页内容：AI Events Around the World in 2026: The Main Annual Meetings To Know\nLast Updated: 14 May 2026\nBy Paulo Palma\nThe real AI conversation happens before the press release. The best AI events of 2026 include NeurIPS, CVPR, AAAI, World Summit AI, and SuperAI Singapore. Credits: NVIDIA\nTABLE OF CONTENTS\nNeurIPS\nICML\nCVPR\nAAAI\nThe AI Summit London\nWorld Summit AI\nNVIDIA GTC\nAI for Good Global Summit\nAi4\nThe AI Conference\nConclusion\nFAQs\nEvery year, AI events bring together researchers, founders, investors, students, company teams, and policymakers. These events are not only for people building models. They also give outsiders a clear look at where AI is going, which tools are getting attention, and which ideas are close to showing up in everyday life.\nSome conferences are heavy on research, with papers, experiments, models, and technical talks. Others feel more like trade shows. You see product demos, business tools, robots, chips, apps, and AI being used in health, education, finance, media, transport, and government.\nThe scale is hard to ignore. In 2023, NeurIPS had 13,307 people attending in person and 3,075 joining virtually. That gives a clear sense of how large these AI gatherings have become.\nFor someone following AI from the outside, these events offer something hard to find elsewhere: a real look at what is being built before it reaches the public. You don’t need to be a machine learning expert to learn something. A good talk or demo usually explains what a team is building, why it is relevant, and which problem they are trying to solve.\nNeurIPS\nNeurIPS is one of the oldest annual machine learning conferences around.\nIt started back in 1987 as a research gathering focused primarily on neural information processing, and since then it has grown and expanded into topics like ML, search engines, voice tools, medical systems, AI-powered translation software, and business applications.\nWithin the event you can find research papers, poster sessions, talks with invited experts, workshops, tutorials, competitions, and in some cases even live demos, which adds a lot to the experience for enthusiasts and professionals alike. Recently, the main topics have revolved around language models, AI agents, generative media, optimization, forecasting, safety, and especially learning methods for teams building real-world systems.\nThe event has built up serious prestige over the years. Major companies like Google DeepMind, Google Research, Microsoft, Meta, NVIDIA, Amazon, and even OpenAI have all been part of it through papers, sponsorships, and research teams attending the event. Google DeepMind alone presented over 100 papers at the 2024 edition.\nEvent details:\nLast date: December 10–15 2024\nLocation: Vancouver, Canada\nWho goes: Researchers, students, engineers, startups, and tech companies\nWhat you see: Talks, papers, demos, workshops, posters, and competitions\nMain topics: Machine learning, language models, AI safety, neural networks, and optimization\nICML\nICML is the AI conference for people who want to understand how machine learning ideas are born before they reach apps, labs, and products. Since 1980, it has focused on the methods behind modern AI, from training models to testing how well they learn.\nA big part of ICML is about the hard work behind machine learning: training models, testing them, finding weak points, and improving how they learn from data. Some sessions are very academic, but the ideas often connect to tools people later see in search, automation, robotics, language apps, and business software.\nIts audience is full of people who care about how AI works under the surface. Researchers, students, engineers, startups, and major labs go there to follow work on language models, agents, reinforcement learning, robotics, model behavior, and safer systems. The 2026 edition is scheduled for Seoul, South Korea.\nEvent details:\nDate: July 6 to 11 2026\nLocation: Seoul, South Korea\nWho goes: Researchers, students, engineers, AI labs, startups, and tech companies\nWhat you see: Research talks, poster sessions, smaller workshops, tutorials, expert discussions, and company booths\nMain topics: Machine learning, language models, AI agents, reinforcement learning, robotics, model testing, and AI safety\nCVPR\nCVPR is the AI event for people who want to learn about the visual AI world. Since 1985, it has focused on computer vision, which means image recognition, video understanding, 3D scenes, movement, faces, objects, and the many ways AI learns from what it can “see.”\nAt CVPR, the work is easier to follow because many ideas can be shown visually. A session may include systems that understand video, rebuild 3D spaces, detect objects, improve images, or connect pictures with text. That makes the event useful for readers who want to see how visual AI works in practice.\nVisual AI is now part of many things people use without thinking about it, from phone cameras to medical scans and robot vision. CVPR gathers the people pushing that work forward, including university teams, product builders, and company labs. The 2026 edition is scheduled for Denver, Colorado.\nEvent details:\nDate: June 3 to 7 2026\nLocation: Denver, Colorado, USA\nWho goes: Researchers, engineers, students, computer vision teams, startups, and product builders\nWhat you see: Visual demos, research sessions, poster presentations, tutorials, workshops, expert talks, and company exhibits\nMain topics: Computer vision, image models, video AI, 3D vision, robotics, visual reasoning, face tracking, and scene understanding\nAAAI\nAAAI is the AI event for people who want to see the full field in one place. Since 1980, it has covered artificial intelligence beyond one trend, with work on reasoning, planning, search, robots, learning systems, ethics, education, and real uses in science and business.\nThe program covers many sides of AI that do not always get attention in public conversations. It includes work on reasoning, planning, decision making, agents, education, ethics, and human use. That wider focus makes the event useful for understanding what AI can do, where it fails, and how people are trying to guide it.\nAAAI attracts people who want to look at AI from more than one angle. Some come for research, others for education, policy, robotics, or applied work. The 2026 edition took place in Singapore, with sessions covering many parts of artificial intelligence instead of chasing one single trend.\nEvent details:\nDate: January 20 to 27 2026\nLocation: Singapore EXPO, Singapore\nWho goes: Researchers, professors, students, engineers, policy people, startups, and AI companies\n...\n\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：全球AI技术大会 2026\n\n网页标题：2026中国人工智能展8月共探人工智能新前沿\n\n网页链接：https://shanghai01260086.11467.com/m/news/15684285.asp\n\n发布时间：2026-05-19T00:00:00+08:00\n\n网页内容：2026中国人工智能展8月共探人工智能新前沿\n\n![](https://img26.11467.com/2026/02-19/1281816292.jpg)\n**AGIC2026深圳国际通用人工智能大会暨展览会：智启未来，共筑全球AI生态新范式**\n时间：2026年8月26日—28日\n地点：深圳国际会展中心（宝安）\n主办单位：\n深圳市人工智能产业协会\n深圳市物联传媒有限公司\n深圳鹏城会展传媒有限公司\n大会背景与战略定位\n在全球人工智能技术加速迭代、通用人工智能（AGI）成为产业变革核心驱动力的背景下，AGIC2026深圳国际通用人工智能大会暨展览会（简称“AGIC2026”）以“智联世界·赋能未来”为主题，立足深圳“全